71-2156-4-S1-S104-1"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Characteristics of extended families used in linkage analysis to identify loci for the number of grams of alcohol consumed per day.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left"><bold>Category</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Sample size</bold><sup>A</sup></td><td align="left"><bold>Mean &#x000b1; SEM (Range)</bold></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">No. of subjects per family</td><td align="center">329</td><td align="left">14.23 &#x000b1; 0.46 (7&#x02013;84)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">No. of drinkers per pedigree</td><td align="center">329</td><td align="left">6.27 &#x000b1; 0.24 (1&#x02013;46)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Age of subjects</td><td align="center">2565</td><td align="left">43.14 &#x000b1; .33 (5&#x02013;83)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Male subjects</td><td align="center">1233</td><td align="left">42.23 &#x000b1; 0.49 (11&#x02013;82)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Female subjects</td><td align="center">1332</td><td align="left">43.97 &#x000b1; 0.46 (5&#x02013;83)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Age of drinkers</td><td align="center">2063</td><td align="left">42.85 &#x000b1; 0.35 (13&#x02013;81)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Male drinkers</td><td align="center">1047</td><td align="left">42.46 &#x000b1; 0.50 (13&#x02013;81)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Female smokers</td><td align="center">1016</td><td align="left">43.25 &#x000b1; 0.50 (13&#x02013;80)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">No. of grams of alcohol consumed per day</td><td align="center">2063</td><td align="left">18.02 &#x000b1; .54 (2&#x02013;537)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Male drinkers</td><td align="center">1047</td><td align="left">24.96 &#x000b1; 0.94 (2&#x02013;537)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Female drinkers</td><td align="center">1016</td><td align="left">10.87 &#x000b1; 0.40 (2&#x02013;139)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>A</sup>The sample sizes in the first two rows are numbers of pedigrees and those in the rest of the table are numbers of individual subjects.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Genomic locations linked to alcohol consumption with a <italic>p</italic>-value &#x0003c; 0.005 across the human genome, as detected by sib-pair analysis using the program SIBPAL (with the w3 option).</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left"><bold>Chromosome</bold></td><td align="left"><bold>Locus(s)</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Map Position (cM)</bold></td><td align="left"><bold><italic>p</italic>-Value</bold></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">9</td><td align="left">GATA89A11</td><td align="center">83.2</td><td align="left">0.00008</td></tr><tr><td align="left">15</td><td align="left">248vc5</td><td align="center">21.1</td><td align="left">0.0011</td></tr><tr><td align="left">16</td><td align="left">GATA11C06</td><td align="center">136.7</td><td align="left">0.0045</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></sec></back></article>